    <encodingDesc>
      <p>Stand-off alignment per Bron ADR 0006. Targets are xml:ids of the planned edition files: sec-NN (GD¹ §), par-NN and par-13b (GD² Par.). Link types: equal | replace | insert | delete | move | split | merge. cert and resp follow TEI usage. Targets are relative to the linkGrp's xml:base, ../data/bavinck/gd/, so they resolve to the edition files by ordinary URI resolution.</p>
      <p>Documented deviation (Bron ADR 0017): an insert or delete link has exactly one target, the unit that exists on one side only. TEI's Schematron rule for link requires two or more targets, so this file is valid against tei_all with this one documented Schematron deviation. Every other link has two or more targets.</p>
      <p>Notes on links follow the linkGrp as note elements whose target points at the link's xml:id, because tei_all defines link as empty and allows no note inside linkGrp.</p>
    </encodingDesc>
  </teiHeader>
